00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.510
between 120

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.878
and 130 million

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.047
over the four day Memorial Day weekend.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:14.981
Now, the film,

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.783
as you may know, sparked controversy

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.151
when casting Halle

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.820
Bailey, a black woman as the new Ariel.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.922
But how his portrayal of Ariel

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.524
has become an inspiration

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.592
for so many black

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.860
and brown girls around the world

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.496
who can finally see themselves again

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.464
once again represented on the screen.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.466
Who could forget the heartwarming videos

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.667
from when the trailer dropped,

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.202
showing their reactions

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.538
to Bailey shooting?

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:41.841
I've I swam

00:00:44.844 --> 00:00:47.881
while here

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.883
so sweet at the premiere in London.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.185
Hell, we got to meet several fans

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:52.685
on the red

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.054
carpet, telling Variety

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.790
she hopes that they know they are worth

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.793
and deserve to be in these spaces.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.828
CNN's senior entertainment reporter

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:02.762
Lisa France

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.164
joining us now here in studio.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.399
Always a treat, as I like to say.

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.301
Let's talk about you know,

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:09.869
why representation matters

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.370
so much,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.604
especially in this

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:14.641
genre of Disney princesses, right?

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:16.309
And what does it mean

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.044
to you to see Harley?

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:19.712
Yeah, I said on social media

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:20.413
that we talk a lot

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.381
about the representation

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.615
for young girls of color,

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:25.218
but for women of color, people of color.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:27.787
I cried the movie meant so much to me,

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:30.123
especially because this country and world

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.392
feel so splintered and torn apart

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.093
right now.

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:36.096
So to see us up on screen in this huge

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.330
Disney production,

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:39.232
which is, I mean, diverse

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:40.133
in and of itself,

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.034
I mean, the cast,

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:41.468
all of our

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:42.602
y'all sisters

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.404
are different nationalities.

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.271
Daveed plays

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:47.340
the crab, you know, he's Afro-Latino.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.375
So I feel like this film,

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.478
Disney's really gotten behind diversity.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.246
It's the promotion for it.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.215
I mean, the promotion budget was huge.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:56.716
So for Little girls of color,

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.084
little boys of color,

00:01:58.084 --> 00:01:59.419
grown women of color,

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.353
grown men of color,

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.254
it's just important

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.123
to have representation right now

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.457
in this era that we're living

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:05.925
in, we're in everything just feels like

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.494
people are so far apart.

00:02:07.494 --> 00:02:08.761
We could all come together

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.029
and rally around this film.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.064
Have you seen it? I have.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:11.531
What do you think

00:02:13.666 --> 00:02:15.034
So take it for what it is.

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:15.301
I know

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.669
a lot of people want to compare it

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.770
to the animated.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:18.071
Yeah,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.406
I feel like they did a really great job.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:20.807
I feel like,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.207
first of all,

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:24.010
I feel like Haley was born to play Oreo.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.212
As soon as you hear her saying her voice.

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.715
In part of your world.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.450
I mean, those final notes.

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.952
There's a great video of her performing

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.287
with the orchestra. I've seen that.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.488
And when she finishes,

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:36.556
she kind of steps back

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.558
